{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"**Creations increase ETF shares outstanding; redemptions decrease them.**\n\n- **Creation:** An authorized participant (AP) delivers the required basket of securities, cash, or both to the ETF. In exchange, the fund issues new shares, typically in large blocks called *creation units*.\n- **Redemption:** An AP returns ETF shares to the fund in exchange for securities, cash, or both. Those shares are canceled, reducing shares outstanding.\n\n**Net change in shares outstanding = shares created − shares redeemed.** If creations and redemptions offset, the share count stays unchanged.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Ordinary exchange trading transfers existing shares between investors—it does not itself change the number outstanding."}}
